From: A5E build validation
Subject: sunxi: update sun55i IOMMU attach_dev callback for Linux 6.18

The iommu_domain_ops.attach_dev callback in Linux 6.18 takes the previous
domain as a third argument. Keep the driver's existing rollback logic,
which tracks the active hardware domain internally, and accept the new
callback signature.

--- a/target/linux/sunxi/files/drivers/iommu/sun55i-iommu.c
+++ b/target/linux/sunxi/files/drivers/iommu/sun55i-iommu.c
@@ -759,10 +759,12 @@
 static int sun55i_iommu_attach_dev(struct iommu_domain *domain,
-\t\t\t\t   struct device *dev)
+\t\t\t\t   struct device *dev,
+\t\t\t\t   struct iommu_domain *old_domain_arg)
 {
 \tstruct sunxi_iommu_domain *sunxi_domain =
 \t\tcontainer_of(domain, struct sunxi_iommu_domain, domain);
 \tstruct sunxi_iommu_domain *old_domain = NULL;
 \tstruct sunxi_iommu_owner *owner = dev_iommu_priv_get(dev);
 \tunsigned long flags;
 \tint ret;
 
+\t(void)old_domain_arg;
+
